  "id": "nord-wave",
  "name": "Nord Wave",
  "manufacturer": "Nord",
  "family": "Wave",
  "status": "experimental",
  "trust": "local",
  "description": "Nord Wave (2007) synthesizer: every control of its manual's MIDI controller list.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "type": "manual",
      "title": "Nord Wave User Manual, OS v2.x, Edition 2.0",
      "notes": "MIDI controller list (page 61 of the PDF) read by tools/profiles/nord/read-nord-cc.mjs from Nord Wave English User Manual v2.x Edition 2.0.pdf (sha256 31de84a08bc768f0a804a39da98ef4c9473bd966a84da2e29fc6968d27ace94d), https://www.nordkeyboards.com/wt/documents/289/Nord%20Wave%20English%20User%20Manual%20v2.x%20Edition%202.0.pdf. Not yet checked against the instrument itself."
    }
  ],
  "testedWith": [],
  "authoringNotes": [
    "Generated by tools/profiles/nord/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/nord/synths/, not this file.",
    "Every parameter is a row of the manual's MIDI controller list, with its printed name, sent as the control change it prints on the channel variable. Nothing here has been sent to a real instrument yet.",
    "The list prints controller numbers only: every value is 0 - 127, and a setting chosen from a list (a model, a waveform, an effect type) is a number here, not a choice.",
    "The manual: an on/off button is 0 off and 127 on; a button that steps through settings starts at 0 and goes up in equal steps. Each Slot, A and B, has its MIDI channel; set the channel variable to the one to edit.",
    "The list's third column, the General MIDI name of each controller number, is kept in the descriptions.",
    "Messages the list gives to two rows, both laid out: CC 17: Oct Shift, Mono Mode. CEditor sends either, and follows neither when the instrument sends it."
  ],
  "variables": {
    "channel": 1
  },
  "coverage": {
    "singleParameterWrite": "complete-for-the-manual's-MIDI-controller-list",
    "realtimeEditing": "complete-for-the-manual's-MIDI-controller-list",
    "editBufferDumpRequest": "notImplemented",
    "editBufferDumpParse": "notImplemented",
    "bankDump": "notImplemented",
    "inboundControllers": "the instrument sends these same messages when its panel is used, where its MIDI settings allow",
    "verifiedOnHardware": false
  },
  "timing": {
    "minDelayBetweenMessagesMs": 0
  },
